<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<title>Synthetic Document</title>
<style>
  @page { size: A4; margin: 0; }
  .page {
    width: 794px; height: 1123px;
    padding: 50px 60px; box-sizing: border-box;
    overflow: hidden; page-break-after: always;
    position: relative;
  }
  .page:last-child { page-break-after: auto; }
  body {
    font-family: "DejaVu Serif", "Liberation Serif", Georgia, "Times New Roman", serif;
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: #333;
  }
  h1, h2, h3, h4 {
    font-family: "DejaVu Sans", "Liberation Sans", Arial, sans-serif;
    margin-top: 0.5em;
    margin-bottom: 0.5em;
  }
  .header-logo {
    font-size: 48px;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .title-text {
    font-size: 24px;
    font-weight: bold;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .subtitle-text {
    font-size: 18px;
    text-align: center;
    margin-bottom: 40px;
  }
  .section-heading {
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: bold;
    margin-top: 30px;
    margin-bottom: 15px;
    border-bottom: 2px solid #ccc;
    padding-bottom: 5px;
  }
  .content-block {
    margin-bottom: 20px;
  }
  .signature-block {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-top: 40px;
  }
  .signature-item {
    text-align: center;
    width: 45%;
  }
  .signature-item img {
    max-width: 150px;
    height: auto;
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .table-container {
    width: 100%;
    border-collapse: collapse;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .table-container th, .table-container td {
    border: 1px solid #ddd;
    padding: 8px;
    text-align: left;
  }
  .table-container th {
    background-color: #f2f2f2;
  }
  .two-column-layout {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 40px;
    margin-top: 20px;
  }
  .two-column-layout > div {
    flex: 1;
  }
  .footer {
    text-align: center;
    margin-top: 50px;
    font-size: 12px;
    color: #777;
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="page">
  <div class="header-logo">
    <span style="font-size: 60px;">UAH</span>
  </div>
  <div class="title-text">
    CIVIL AND ENVIRONMENTAL ENGINEERING
  </div>
  <div class="subtitle-text">
    THE UNIVERSITY OF ALABAMA IN HUNTSVILLE
  </div>

  <div class="section-heading">
    CHAIR'S MESSAGE
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>I am very excited to share this issue of our newsletter with you to give you an update on the progress of the Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering at UAH. In this edition, I would like to share with you a number of activities in research and education taking place within the department. We are pleased to welcome <span data-field="new_faculty_member_name">Dr. {{ new_faculty_member_name }}</span> and <span data-field="new_faculty_member_name_2">Dr. {{ new_faculty_member_name_2 }}</span> to our department. Dr. <span data-field="faculty_member_name">Dr. {{ faculty_member_name }}</span> received his Bachelor's degree in Structural Engineering from <span data-field="undergrad_institution">University of {{ undergrad_institution }}</span> in <span data-field="undergrad_year">{{ undergrad_year }}</span> and his M.S. and Ph.D. from <span data-field="grad_institution">{{ grad_institution }}</span>. His research area is in structural and in-frastructural materials. Dr. <span data-field="faculty_member_name_2">Dr. {{ faculty_member_name_2 }}</span> earned his Ph.D. in Environmental Engineering from the <span data-field="phd_institution">University of {{ phd_institution }}</span> in <span data-field="phd_year">{{ phd_year }}</span>. She received her Bachelor's and Master's degrees from <span data-field="undergrad_institution_2">{{ undergrad_institution_2 }}</span>, China and the <span data-field="grad_institution_2">{{ grad_institution_2 }}</span>, respectively. Most recently, she worked as a postdoctoral associate at the <span data-field="postdoc_institution">{{ postdoc_institution }}</span> focusing on the development of design principles for low-energy and low-emissions net-zero water buildings of the future.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-block">
    <p>Our faculty continues to excel in research, conducting cutting-edge research in many areas and earning national recognition. Our faculty receives funding from <span data-field="funding_agency_1">{{ funding_agency_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="funding_agency_2">{{ funding_agency_2 }}</span>, <span data-field="funding_agency_3">{{ funding_agency_3 }}</span>, and <span data-field="funding_agency_4">{{ funding_agency_4 }}</span>. Our graduates continue to have a wide range of opportunities that exist on many fronts. Some of the companies who have recruited our students include the <span data-field="company_1">{{ company_1 }}</span>, <span data-field="company_2">{{ company_2 }}</span> officer programs, the <span data-field="company_3">{{ company_3 }}</span>, the <span data-field="company_4">{{ company_4 }}</span>, and <span data-field="company_5">{{ company_5 }}</span>, and the <span data-field="company_6">{{ company_6 }}</span>. Our ASCE Student Chapter continues to be active and humming.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="signature-block">
    <div class="signature-item">
      <img src="placeholder_image_1.png" alt="Houssam Toutanji">
      <p>Houssam Toutanji,<br>Chair and Professor</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">
    Staff News
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>The Department of Civil and Environmental Engineering and the College of Engineering at UAH is also pleased to welcome <span data-field="new_staff_member_name">{{ new_staff_member_name }}</span> as the new Staff Assistant in the Civil & Environmental Engineering Department. Gabby comes to CEE from a stint as an Event Coordinator at <span data-field="previous_employer">{{ previous_employer }}</span>, and she is a highly organized and enthusiastic individual. Gabby has been with the university for several years living in Asia and Europe with her children and husband. Gabby is a retired Army Officer. Gabby previously served as the Executive Secretary for the Dean of the University of <span data-field="previous_university">{{ previous_university }}</span> College of Design, Computer Science and Media Communications in Wisconsin. Gabby has a background in event planning, administration, and communications. Gabby is a graduate of the <span data-field="previous_school">University of {{ previous_school }}</span> in <span data-field="previous_year">{{ previous_year }}</span>. Gabby is a graduate of the <span data-field="previous_school_2">University of {{ previous_school_2 }}</span>. Gabby is a graduate of the <span data-field="previous_school_3">University of {{ previous_school_3 }}</span>. Gabby is a graduate of the <span data-field="previous_school_4">University of {{ previous_school_4 }}</span>.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column-layout">
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_2.png" alt="Gabrielle Cromartie">
        <p>Gabrielle Cromartie</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_3.png" alt="Dr. Tingting Wu">
        <p>Dr. Tingting Wu</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="section-heading">
    New Faculty Profiles
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>The College of Engineering at UAH is very pleased to welcome <span data-field="new_faculty_name">{{ new_faculty_name }}</span>, appointed as Assistant Professor of Civil and Environmental Engineering in August 2014. Her doctoral research focused on the development and evaluation of engineered media that can be utilized to remove dissolved phosphorus in urban waters from both point source and non-point source. Most recently, she worked as a postdoctoral associate at the <span data-field="postdoc_institution_2">{{ postdoc_institution_2 }}</span> focusing on the development of design principles for low-energy, low-emissions net-zero water buildings of the future. Her research interests include sustainable water/wastewater treatment and reuse, advanced water treatment, and stormwater/non-point source pollution control.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-block">
    <p>Dr. <span data-field="faculty_member_name_3">Dr. {{ faculty_member_name_3 }}</span> earned his Ph.D. in Environmental Engineering from the <span data-field="phd_institution_3">{{ phd_institution_3 }}</span> in <span data-field="phd_year_3">{{ phd_year_3 }}</span>. He received his Bachelor's and M.S. from <span data-field="undergrad_institution_3">{{ undergrad_institution_3 }}</span>, China and the <span data-field="grad_institution_3">{{ grad_institution_3 }}</span>, respectively.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column-layout">
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_4.png" alt="Dr. Tingting Wu">
        <p>Dr. Tingting Wu</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_5.png" alt="Dr. Hongyu Zhou">
        <p>Dr. Hongyu Zhou</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">
    Student Graduate Projects & Dissertations
  </div>
  <div class="table-container">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Name</th>
        <th>Title</th>
        <th>Advisor</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in student_projects %}
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="student_projects[{{ loop.index0 }}].name">{{ item.name }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="student_projects[{{ loop.index0 }}].title">{{ item.title }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="student_projects[{{ loop.index0 }}].advisor">{{ item.advisor }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </div>

  <div class="section-heading">
    Civil Engineering Program Outstanding Graduate Student for 2014
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p><span data-field="award_recipient_name">{{ award_recipient_name }}</span>, a native of <span data-field="recipient_hometown">{{ recipient_hometown }}</span>, was attracted to the University of Alabama in Huntsville due to its strong engineering school, provision of the opportunity to personally contribute to research advances, as well as its desirable location within the state. Stephanie is sincerely honored to be recognized with the Civil Engineering Program Outstanding Graduate Student Award 2014.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-heading">
    Faculty Publications
  </div>
  <div class="table-container">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Author(s)</th>
        <th>Title</th>
        <th>Journal/Source</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in faculty_publications %}
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="faculty_publications[{{ loop.index0 }}].authors">{{ item.authors }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="faculty_publications[{{ loop.index0 }}].title">{{ item.title }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="faculty_publications[{{ loop.index0 }}].source">{{ item.source }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">
    Student Profiles
  </div>
  <div class="two-column-layout">
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_6.png" alt="Zhenglai Shen">
        <p><span data-field="profile_name">{{ profile_name }}</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p><span data-field="profile_text">{{ profile_text }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_7.png" alt="Paisley Marotta">
        <p><span data-field="profile_name_2">{{ profile_name_2 }}</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p><span data-field="profile_text_2">Paisley Marotta is a first year graduate student at UAH. Originally from <span data-field="profile_hometown_2">{{ profile_text_2">Paisley Marotta is a first year graduate student at UAH. Originally from <span data-field= }}</span>, she has been studying at UAH for many years. Paisley graduated with a Bachelor's degree from the University of Alabama at Birmingham (UAB) in 2012. Soon after graduation, she moved to Kansas to work for a government contractor. She was responsible for data management. Her drive to do more engineering related work her back to Huntsville to pursue her Master's degree at UAH.</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="two-column-layout">
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_8.png" alt="Matthew Hussak">
        <p><span data-field="profile_name_3">{{ profile_name_3 }}</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p><span data-field="profile_text_3">{{ profile_text_3 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div>
      <div class="signature-item">
        <img src="placeholder_image_9.png" alt="Dr. Ashraf Al-Hamdan">
        <p><span data-field="profile_name_4">{{ profile_name_4 }}</span></p>
      </div>
      <div class="content-block">
        <p><span data-field="profile_text_4">{{ profile_text_4 }}</span></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">
    Faculty Research Grants/Contracts
  </div>
  <div class="table-container">
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Faculty Member</th>
        <th>Project Title</th>
        <th>Funding Source</th>
        <th>Amount</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      {% for item in research_grants %}
      <tr>
        <td><span data-field="research_grants[{{ loop.index0 }}].faculty_member">{{ item.faculty_member }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="research_grants[{{ loop.index0 }}].title">{{ item.title }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="research_grants[{{ loop.index0 }}].source">{{ item.source }}</span></td>
        <td><span data-field="research_grants[{{ loop.index0 }}].amount">{{ item.amount }}</span></td>
      </tr>
      {% endfor %}
    </tbody>
  </div>

  <div class="section-heading">
    UAH College of Engineering Outstanding Faculty Teaching Award
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p><span data-field="award_description">{{ award_description }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-heading">
    UAH Steel Bridge team competes at Southeast Regional Competition for the first time, finishing overall at eleven out of 24 universities competed
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p><span data-field="bridge_team_summary">{{ bridge_team_summary }}</span></p>
    <p><span data-field="bridge_team_future">{{ bridge_team_future }}</span></p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-block">
    <img src="placeholder_image_10.png" alt="Bridge Competition">
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">
    Outstanding Alumni of Civil Engineering Program
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <div class="two-column-layout">
      <div>
        <div class="signature-item">
          <img src="placeholder_image_11.png" alt="Jacqueline Marriott Wilson">
          <p><span data-field="alumni_name">{{ alumni_name }}</span></p>
        </div>
        <div class="content-block">
          <p><span data-field="alumni_bio">{{ alumni_bio }}</span></p>
          <p><span data-field="alumni_career">{{ alumni_career }}</span></p>
          <p><span data-field="alumni_personal">{{ alumni_personal }}</span></p>
          <p><span data-field="alumni_family">{{ alumni_family }}</span></p>
          <p><span data-field="alumni_goals">{{ alumni_goals }}</span></p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">
    $1.2 million driving simulator finds home in UAH's College of Engineering
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <img src="placeholder_image_12.png" alt="Driving Simulator Exterior">
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>The University of Alabama in Huntsville is pleased to announce the arrival of a brand-new high-tech driving simulator, which will be used to provide hands-on training to rural transit operators throughout the state.</p>
    <p>Known as RIDE (Real-Time Instruction for Driver Education), the simulator is funded by a $1.2 million grant from Alabama Department of Transportation (ALDOT) and will be located outside of <span data-field="location_city">{{ location_city }}</span> on the UAH campus. Its operation will be overseen by the Department of Civil & Environmental Engineering in the College of Engineering.</p>
    <p>"We are really excited to be able to offer this training opportunity to rural transit operators in Alabama, who provide an important service to underserved populations living in less accessible areas of the state," says <span data-field="speaker_name">{{ speaker_name }}</span>, associate professor and coordinator of the RIDE program. "We hope to one day expand it to include the many state agencies that also provide transportation to the elderly and disabled."</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-block">
    <p>The simulator's curriculum will include decision driving, close-quarters maneuvering, negotiating intersections, and night/fog driving, all with the goal of reducing accidents and increasing safety.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="signature-block">
    <div class="signature-item">
      <img src="placeholder_image_13.png" alt="Dr. Michael Anderson">
      <p>Dr. Michael Anderson</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
  <div class="section-heading">
    $1.2 million driving simulator finds home in UAH's College of Engineering (Contd.)
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <img src="placeholder_image_14.png" alt="Driving Simulator Interior">
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>RIDE Driving Simulator - Inside View</p>
    <p>Ing passenger and driver safety. Additional scenarios can also be developed on an as-needed basis using RIDE's non-mobile companion simulator, which will be housed in the Department of Civil & Environmental Engineering.</p>
    <p>"RIDE would not have been possible without the support we've received from ALDOT, and we look forward to partnering with them on this educational outreach initiative," says <span data-field="speaker_name_2">{{ speaker_name_2 }}</span>, adding those interested in scheduling training can call the program's direct line at 256.824.RIDE (7433) or email their request to RIDE@uah.edu.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="content-block">
    <p>For more details on RIDE, please contact:</p>
    <p>Dr. Michael Anderson<br>256.824.RIDE (7433)</p>
    <p>Diana LaChance<br>256.824.6878</p>
    <p>RIDE@uah.edu<br>diana.lachance@uah.edu</p>
  </div>

  <div class="section-heading">
    CEE Department Contact Details
  </div>
  <div class="content-block">
    <p>Dr. Houssam Toutanji, Professor and Chair / Gabrielle Cromartie, Staff Assistant;</p>
    <p>Phone: 256-824-6854; http://www.uah.edu/eng/departments/cee</p>
  </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>